  "oneLinerQuestion": "Design a key-value data structure that stores values at specific timestamps and retrieves them efficiently.",
  "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/time-based-key-value-store/",
  "explanation": "Store key mapping to list of [value, timestamp] pairs. Since timestamps are strictly increasing, use binary search to locate highest timestamp <= targetTimestamp.",
  "pseudoCode": "CLASS TimeMap:\n    CONSTRUCTOR(): store = HASH_MAP()\n    FUNCTION set(key, value, timestamp):\n        IF key NOT IN store THEN store[key] = []\n        APPEND [value, timestamp] TO store[key]\n    FUNCTION get(key, timestamp):\n        res = '', values = store[key] OR []\n        l = 0, r = LENGTH(values) - 1\n        WHILE l <= r DO:\n            m = (l + r) / 2\n            IF values[m][1] <= timestamp THEN res = values[m][0]; l = m + 1\n            ELSE r = m - 1\n        END WHILE\n        RETURN res\nEND CLASS",
